- Remember what others endure for worse ends. Lovers, money seekers, and fame seekers suffer willingly. Acrobats risk death for small pay. It is shameful not to endure as much for virtue (Lectures VII).

- Put your effort in the right place. Instead of working to win another man's wife, work to govern your desires. Instead of working for money, train yourself to want little. Instead of chasing fame, work to stop wanting it. Instead of plotting against someone you envy, learn not to envy (Lectures VII).

- Accept that every good is won by toil. The man unwilling to work hard shows himself unworthy of any good (Lectures VII).$q$, 107, $q$original$q$, $q$https://github.com/Kylejemery/arete-app/blob/main/academy/corpus-ingestion/synthesis/virtues-of-socrates.v1.md$q$, 2026, $q$synthesis$q$, $q$synthesis$q$, $q$english$q$, $q$Intermediate$q$, array[$q$corpus_verified$q$]::text[], true),
