Epictetus divided the whole of training into three areas: what to desire and avoid, how to act toward others, and how to keep your judgment from being deceived (Discourses III.2). The rules are grouped the same way, after the foundation they all rest on.$q$, 44, $q$original$q$, $q$https://github.com/Kylejemery/arete-app/blob/main/academy/corpus-ingestion/synthesis/virtues-of-socrates.v1.md$q$, 2026, $q$synthesis$q$, $q$synthesis$q$, $q$english$q$, $q$Intermediate$q$, array[$q$corpus_verified$q$]::text[], true),
