- Choose a character and keep it. Set yourself a way of being that you hold to alone and in company (Handbook 33).

- Be mostly silent. Say what is necessary, in few words (Handbook 33).

- Leave the common topics alone. Do not talk much about sports, food, or drink, and above all do not talk about other people, praising, blaming, or comparing (Handbook 33).

- Laugh little and swear no oaths. Let your laughter be neither loud nor frequent, and avoid oaths as far as you can (Handbook 33).

- Choose your company. Avoid vulgar entertainments. However clean you are, bad company will soil you (Handbook 33).

- Answer slander with humility. If told someone speaks ill of you, do not defend yourself. Say, "He did not know my other faults, or he would have mentioned those too" (Handbook 33).

- Do not tell your own war stories. Your adventures please you more than they please your listeners. Do not play the clown, and show plainly that you dislike indecent talk (Handbook 33).

- Meet the powerful unmoved. Before going to someone important, expect to be turned away or ignored. If it is your duty to go, go, and never say afterward that it was not worth it. Ask how Socrates or Zeno would behave (Handbook 33).

- At games and shows, want only what happens. No shouting, no jeering, and little talk about it afterward (Handbook 33).

- Do not call yourself a philosopher. At a dinner, do not lecture on how to eat; eat as you ought. Sheep do not bring up their grass to show the shepherd how much they ate; they turn it into wool and milk (Handbook 46).

- Be content to be thought a fool. About externals, accept looking foolish. If someone tells you that you know nothing and it does not sting, you have begun (Handbook 13, 46).

- Expect to be mocked when you start. People will sneer at your new seriousness. Hold steady, and those who laughed will come to respect you (Handbook 22).$q$, 333, $q$original$q$, $q$https://github.com/Kylejemery/arete-app/blob/main/academy/corpus-ingestion/synthesis/virtues-of-socrates.v1.md$q$, 2026, $q$synthesis$q$, $q$synthesis$q$, $q$english$q$, $q$Intermediate$q$, array[$q$corpus_verified$q$]::text[], true)
